From a7a3a2501c4a18b8384fc519e93e80354e522cb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Valery Petrov <valerypetrov@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 03:26:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Check the local shard's own grants before the prometheus
 shard probe

The shard probe of a prometheus read runs on the server's own context,
after the wrapper's SELECT and READ ON REMOTE. A shard that is this
server itself is read in-process on the caller's context instead: the
generated cluster() call resolves its view() here, and the selector in
it enforces SELECT on the shard-local table and CREATE TEMPORARY TABLE
only then. A caller holding the wrapper's grants but not those was
answered by the probe with UNEXPECTED_TABLE_ENGINE or TYPE_MISMATCH
about the shard-local table instead of a plain access error.

Require both before the probe whenever the cluster has a local shard,
resolving the table as the selector does: in the caller's current
database when the wrapper declares none. The tests give a user every
grant but one over a wrapper whose local shard resolves to a MergeTree
table for that user, so the leak is present to be leaked, and assert
the refusal names the missing grant and nothing about the shard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016i1XnLC3KypZdaYYsfzqub
---
